  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:97562",
  "description": "The skopeo command lets you inspect images from container image registries, get images and image layers, and use signatures to create and verify files.   \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * net: golang: Go net package: Denial of Service via long CNAME response in LookupCNAME (CVE-2026-33811)\n  * docker: Moby/Docker Engine: Arbitrary Code Execution via malicious container image and compressed archive upload (CVE-2026-41567)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * Update skopeo to 1.22.2 [rhel-9.9] (JIRA:RHEL-170520)\n  * update to the latest upstream release (JIRA:RHEL-185740)\n  * switch skopeo to sustaining-engineering GitLab release-1.22 branch and bump epoch (JIRA:RHEL-220456)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.  \n\nAdditional Changes:  \n\nFor detailed information on changes in this release, see the AlmaLinux 9 Release Notes linked from the References section.\n",
